The bug in `sum.mjs` is that the loop starts from index 1 instead of 0. This means it skips the first element of the array when calculating the total.

To fix this, we need to change the loop to start from index 0:

```javascript
export function sum(nums) {
  let total = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) { // Change i = 1 to i = 0
    total += nums[i];
  }
  return total;
}

console.log(sum([10, 20, 30]));
```

